{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542235-other-supernatural-interactions-in-your-games","id":1542235,"title":"Other supernatural interactions in your games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-16T01:35:36-07:00","id":1542235,"title":"Other supernatural interactions in your games","content":"So my main ST likes his games to be separate but does claim all options are available (werewolves, mages, demons etc) if the players wish to persue them for some reason. Now, my Ventrue is in need of some muscle and I am kind of thinking of trying my luck outside of other kindred by attempting to contact other groups.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty much after ideas on how this may be approached correctly by hearing what other players have done and if they've made successful but not lethal contact with other groups<br /> <br /> I have an idea to hopefully get a Werewolf on the payroll by hunting down where one lives and then ONLY making contact via a burner phone I deliver while offering them cash to have them go &quot;deal&quot; with kindred I want dead and my 5 resources Ventrue has recently purchased an occult bookstore that I am hoping with my semi decent occult knowledge will allow me to find a way to attract someone with genuine magical abilities but yeah, anyone have some success stories to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27150-minnzy","name":"Minnzy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T15:00:14-07:00","id":1542275,"title":"","content":"It wasn't for VTM, but it was with Changeling the Lost where we had Fireheart that was a childhood friend of a Ventrue ancillae that started to keep in touch when the Elemental escaped Arcadia and over time they would do odd jobs for each other periodically.<br /> <br /> But it was an uneasy relationship as the Fireheart got older and more powerful and closer to his Fae side and you would see bleed through the mien and the Ventrue would see it and get somewhat fearful.<br /> <br /> So perhaps a personal connection could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  I hate needless autocorrect. 09-16-2024, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T19:47:45-07:00","id":1542287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542235-other-supernatural-interactions-in-your-games?p=1542275#post1542275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't for VTM, but it was with Changeling the Lost where we had Fireheart that was a childhood friend of a Ventrue ancillae that started to keep in touch when the Elemental escaped Arcadia and over time they would do odd jobs for each other periodically.<br /> <br /> But it was an uneasy relationship as the Fireheart got older and more powerful and closer to his Face side and you would see bleed through the mien and the Ventrue would see it and get somewhat fearful.<br /> <br /> So perhaps a personal connection could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a pretty sweet storyline you had. I'd have loved to start with something like that actually but that's a &quot;Knowing what I know now&quot; thing because I made my character thinking all that stuff would be easier to acquire in game... boy was I wrong. Having a Ventrue start with no contacts or allies makes for a real struggle as a &quot;Social&quot; character so forming connections isn't something I'm having much luck in. Damn, my real life has leaked too much in to my roleplay life! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27150-minnzy","name":"Minnzy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T11:46:01-07:00","id":1542329,"title":"","content":"It was an interesting storyline and seeing the Ventrue seeing how strange his Fireheart friend was getting as the power of his Wyrd increased and became more like the element he was turned into was a good subplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T14:50:00-07:00","id":1542337,"title":"","content":"The involvement of other supernatural creatures in a Vampire chronicle is something that is really up to the ST, not players.<br /> <br /> Personally as ST I do like to figure out what any major supernatural creatures in a city might be doing and how they might encounter vampires, but I want any interactions with them to be something that adds an appropriate feel to a vampire game rather than distract from it.<br /> <br /> I also think werewolf and vampires should be able to interact with each other in some capacity despite them being enemies for the most part. There are lots of ways this can be done that makes sense in both a Werewolf and Vampire setting. You just need to be careful about how you justify and develop it. <br /> <br /> But what about as a player?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minnzy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542235-other-supernatural-interactions-in-your-games#post1542235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty much after ideas on how this may be approached correctly by hearing what other players have done and if they've made successful but not lethal contact with other groups</div> </div> </div> </div>So much depends on your ST sees werewolves and develops individual werewolves in his game. Something that works for one ST won't work for another, and even something that works in one chronicle for an ST might now work for a different chronicle run by the same ST because too many details are different.<br /> <br /> A general statement is that your character needs to find those werewolves who do not automatically try to kill every vampire they encounter. The good news is that any werewolves in a city are the ones most likely to do that. The bad news is that they may still kill you later. Bone Gnawers often don't follow the Litany. Both Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers are prone to tolerate vampires in order to concentrate on other threats. Select werewolves from other tribes might have their own justifications for cooperation with vampires, for example Shadow Lords of the Bringers of Light camp who would say they are &quot;testing&quot; themselves by being around vampires and not becoming corrupt. There could be Ronin who do not see destroying vampires as part of a religious obligation. And there could be individual werewolves or packs who are some measure of naive, corrupt, stupid, or cunning that would be willing to do so.<br /> <br /> The problem is trying to find them while not getting killed.<br /> <br /> So the first thing I would do is try to find other vampires who might already know some and provide intel first before I do anything else. In the game this would likely be a member of the Gangrel or Nosferatu. They may or may not know anything, but I'd check with them first. The second thing I would do is read and analyze news that could indicate areas of likely werewolf activity. Are there areas vampires already avoid because it's too dangerous? Are there reports of savagely killed humans, particularly if they are concentrated in a geographic area? Once I have some combination of intelligence that gives me a place to look, I then begin my own research in the area - hopefully in a way that protects me even if certain retainers, allies, pawns, etc. are lost.<br /> <br /> Only after I do all this research would I think of the best way to safely make direct contact and try to negotiate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minnzy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1542235-other-supernatural-interactions-in-your-games#post1542235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea to hopefully get a Werewolf on the payroll by hunting down where one lives and then ONLY making contact via a burner phone I deliver while offering them cash to have them go &quot;deal&quot; with kindred I want dead and my 5 resources Ventrue has recently purchased an occult bookstore that I am hoping with my semi decent occult knowledge will allow me to find a way to attract someone with genuine magical abilities but yeah, anyone have some success stories to share?</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes a lot of assumptions that may get your character killed. Even if you can identify a werewolf somehow, why do you think some random werewolf would want to help you? Why do you think that werewolf cares so much about money they would do your bidding?<br /> <br /> You probably need to learn a lot more information about any specific werewolf first before you make contact and before you negotiate. Try to figure out what that werewolf actually wants that you can provide and which that werewolf cannot get elsewhere. Only after you do that should you attempt to make contact and negotiate. Otherwise the answer could be &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> Expect to spend a lot more time doing investigation before you even get to the point of negotiation.<br /> <br /> = =<br /> As for mages, it's much more likely the mage will be aware of you before you ever become aware of the mage. Any information you can get from an occult bookstore or routine occult knowledge will probably not help you. At most, you would want to plant a trusted ghoul or other retainer in the occult scene, or recruit someone who is already inside, and hope that some night that person uncovers something that may be able to help you identify and negotiate with a mage. And prepare to be rejected because it's very likely you can't offer the mage anything she finds useful.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> Typically you will need to spend a long time just hoping to find such creatures, and then a long time earning trust with them with small scale mutual favors before you can even think about asking in major favors or paying for services. Supernatural creatures in general don't need money, and they have more important things to be someone else's muscle or acting as an assassin for them. They should be major NPCs in their own right with their own goals. They just don't do favors for random people they encounter. They are not a plumber who helps anyone who calls them and offers money. If they are willing to help, it's only for those creatures who can be counted as loyal allies, who have personal ties with them, and can help them achieve their own goals as well. It's about building some kind of mutually beneficial relationship even if it has to be one of limited scope.<br /> <br /> That is how I would run such encounters as an ST. Other STs may be different.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T17:17:13-07:00","id":1542402,"title":"","content":"That is a good point is how are you able to explain how the partnership even happens as most of the time all the various supernatural communities keep away from each other. Most kindred outside of the Gangrel or even the Ventrue or Banu Haqim are fearful of lupines and want nothing to do with them. Most lupines view the undead as disgusting freaks who first, second and third thought is to turn them into greasy ashes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T19:40:36-07:00","id":1542472,"title":"","content":"Among the various supernatural groups, I think your best option is to go out for Changelings.<br /> <br /> Fairies have the least hostile attitude to Vampires, and some of them can be pretty strong. Not as strong as a Werewolf most of the time, but very strong nonetheless. Many of them would love to have a relationship with a vampire just for the thrill of it. Your best chances and reward would probably be to befriend a Redcap.<br /> <br /> But almost everything said by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> still stands. You need information, avoid making assumptions, and don\u2019t think you can simply buy your way with one of them. Changelings have their own host of problems and priorities, as their own society. They can also be incredibly dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}